// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6659 new: Transparent Tribe (APT36) PcDirvs loader, public core HTA and Crimson RAT runner
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6659
// Pull request author: sohankanna
// Change: new rule
// Title: Transparent Tribe Crimson RAT Batch Runner Execution
// Sigma ID: fa72336f-17ea-4e5e-a7d6-df6585635cfe
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: @sohankanna
// Date: 2026-11-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1204.002, T1059.003, G0134
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects the execution of the "mycsd.bat" runner script used by Transparent Tribe (APT36) to
//   deploy Crimson RAT, as reported by Acronis TRU in February 2026. In this campaign against Indian
//   startups, an ISO ("MeetBisht.iso") contains a LNK disguised as an Excel file ("Meet
//   Bisht.xlsx.lnk"). The LNK starts the batch script minimised via "%COMSPEC% /c start /MIN", which
//   shows a decoy spreadsheet, removes the Mark of the Web and launches Crimson RAT.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.acronis.com/en/tru/posts/new-year-new-sector-transparent-tribe-targets-indias-startup-ecosystem/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/0d96dbbaf239f29b10f0dea2f2a15c27dcbb3659/rules-emerging-threats/2026/TA/Transparent-Tribe/proc_creation_win_apt_transparent_tribe_crimson_rat_runner.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "Cmd.Exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "start " and ProcessCommandLine contains "/MIN" and ProcessCommandLine contains "mycsd.bat")
